<article class="env-lemma" id="069D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/069D">Lemma <span data-tag="069D">37.61.14</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(f) =$“$f$ is perfect” is fppf local on the source. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\{ g_ i : X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ be an fppf covering of schemes and let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism such that each $f \circ g_ i$ is perfect. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0699" data-tag="0699">37.60.13</a> we conclude that $f$ is pseudo-coherent. Hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/069C" data-tag="069C">37.61.11</a> it suffices to check that $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is an $\mathcal{O}_{S, f(x)}$-module of finite tor dimension for all $x \in X$. Pick $i \in I$ and $x_ i \in X_ i$ mapping to $x$. Then we see that $\mathcal{O}_{X_ i, x_ i}$ has finite tor dimension over $\mathcal{O}_{S, f(x)}$ and that $\mathcal{O}_{X, x} \to \mathcal{O}_{X_ i, x_ i}$ is faithfully flat. The desired conclusion follows from More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/068S" data-tag="068S">15.68.17</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>